   A second embedded recipe, `contracts/recipes/darn-recipe.yaml`, drives a darn run: one gated `Darn-Write` writer that writes and validates the decision record first and, once its `discussion` gate passes, commits it, then reads the board entry, edits, tests and commits, then the `Darn-Review` perch (`Darn-Bouncer`, `Darn-Burler-Review` and `Darn-Burler-Fix`) reviews the committed diff against the board entry as amended by the record's `Added after Discussion` entries and carries its open findings into the record, then `Describe` rewrites the change description from the final diff, then Merge-In, Publish, PR-Align, PR-Gate and Finalize, with no discussion, plan, webster or merge-review rows.
-  The perch's bounce budget is `darn.yaml`'s `review_max_bounces`, default `1`, and `0` routes `Darn-Write` straight to Merge-In, so the writer's own description stands; its hard cap is `review_hard_max_bounces`, default `4`, and `review_amend_max_bounces` is the amendment allowance a re-entered review of a changed subject runs under.
+  The perch's bounce budget is `darn.yaml`'s `review_max_bounces`, default `1`, and `0` routes `Darn-Write` straight to Merge-In, so the writer's own description stands; its hard cap is `review_hard_max_bounces`, default `2`, and `review_amend_max_bounces` is the amendment allowance a re-entered review of a changed subject runs under.
   All three are settable per run through the task's `run_settings`.
   `darn_reviewer_model` and `darn_fixer_model` set the perch's reviewer and fixer models, an empty one taking `loom.yaml`'s `reviewer_model` or `fixer_model`.
   `darn_reviewer_fan` and `darn_fixer_fan` give the perch a per-round lens fan and twill fixer, empty by default and closed to the local layer.
